            <ArticleTitle>A randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial of acetazolamide for the treatment of elevated intracranial pressure in cryptococcal meningitis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>769-72</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We conducted a trial of oral acetazolamide for the treatment of cryptococcal meningitis in 22 Thai adults with headache and an opening cerebrospinal fluid pressure of &gt;/=200 mm H(2)0. The trial was terminated prematurely because patients who received acetazolamide developed significantly lower venous bicarbonate levels and higher chloride levels and had more-frequent serious adverse events than did subjects who received placebo.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
